FigFlow is built on top of the Origin-independent analytical core of EditaPlot.
Per the Apache License 2.0, this NOTICE retains the original copyright and
records the following changes:

1. Reused (largely unmodified) modules: table ingestion and validation,
   column-role inference / scientific preparation, template specifications,
   plot-plan construction, scientific palettes, and the matplotlib-based
   publication preview renderer.
2. Removed and not redistributed: the Origin/OriginPro automation backend
   (originpro / COM session), the desktop GUI (PySide6), background workers,
   and per-template Origin runner/service entry points.
3. Changed behavior: rendering is performed entirely by the bundled
   matplotlib engine and writes editable SVG plus high-resolution PNG/PDF.
   FigFlow does not create Origin projects (.opju) and does not launch,
   install, or require Origin or OriginPro.
4. Added: the FigFlow application layer (CLI, deterministic intent-aware
   chart selector, renderer orchestration) and a one-click local setup.

